{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 disproof of Erdős Problem 549 in the form stated by Formal Conjectures: it is not true that every tree T with k vertices in one class and 2k in the other has diagonal Ramsey number R(T) = 4k − 1. The witness is k = 4 and the double star S(3,7), whose centres have 3 and 7 leaves, with classes of sizes 4 and 8. An explicit 2-colouring of the edges of K₁₅ contains no monochromatic copy, so R(T) ≥ 16 > 15. The colouring is checked by the Lean kernel.",
